Assumption: you're asking about the classic "Leaders in an Array" problem (an element is a leader if it is greater than every element to its right). Scan from right to left, tracking the maximum seen so far.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public static class LeadersInArray
{
    public static List<long> FindLeaders(long[] arr)
    {
        var leaders = new List<long>();
        if (arr == null || arr.Length == 0) return leaders;

        long max = long.MinValue;
        for (int i = arr.Length - 1; i >= 0; i--)
        {
            if (arr[i] > max)
            {
                leaders.Add(arr[i]);
                max = arr[i];
            }
        }
        leaders.Reverse();
        return leaders;
    }
}
```

Time: O(n). Space: O(k) for the output list, where k is the number of leaders.

